---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "~/components/Icon.astro";
import { GITHUB } from "~/data/nav";

const articles = [
  {
    title: "A person is not an account.",
    text: [
      "We are a colleague, a parent, a neighbour and a stranger on a forum, sometimes within the same hour. None of these is a mask, and none is the real one hiding behind the others.",
      "A system that allows one account per person is describing its database. It is not describing people.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "The self is private.",
    text: [
      "Behind the identities there is someone who chooses between them. That someone signs in, and is seen by no one else.",
      "The private self has no profile page, no public name and no identifier to hand out. It is not concealed data. It is simply nobody else's business.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Identities are declared, not deduced.",
    text: [
      "An identity says what you wrote in it: a name, a picture, a few words. Nothing is inferred, scored or completed on your behalf.",
      "When a system knows more about one of your identities than you told it, that identity has stopped being yours.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Separation is built in, or it is not there.",
    text: [
      "A privacy policy is a promise, and promises change with owners. Keeping two identities apart has to follow from how the system is made, so that it holds on the days when nobody is being careful.",
      "A website should be unable to connect what it knows of you to anything else, because the connection exists nowhere it can reach.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "No passwords.",
    text: [
      "A password is a secret people are asked to invent, remember and never reuse, hundreds of times over. They cannot, and that is not their failing.",
      "A passkey asks for a gesture instead. There will be no password added just in case.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Your server, or one you chose.",
    text: [
      "Somebody has to know which identities are yours: the server that signs you in. So that server should answer to you.",
      "brig·id is software to run, not a service to join. There is no central registry, no company account, and nothing for anyone to acquire.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Open, so that it can be checked.",
    text: [
      "The code, the specifications and the decisions are public, with their reasons and their wrong turns. The cryptography is chosen to last, classical and post-quantum together.",
      "“Trust us” is not an argument. “Here is how to verify” is.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Say what is not built.",
    text: [
      "This project is young. Part of what this site describes exists, part is being written, part is a plan. Every claim carries its label, and the limits are written next to the promises.",
      "An identity system that oversells itself has already failed at its only job.",
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Manifesto"
  description="Eight principles behind brig·id: a person is not an account, the self is private, identities are declared, and separation has to be built in."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Manifesto</p>
      <h1>
        You are <span class="accent spectrum">plural.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        brig·id starts from an observation and a refusal. The observation: a
        person is several people, and always was. The refusal: letting whoever
        owns the sign-in button decide otherwise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <ol class="shell-narrow articles">
      {articles.map((article, index) => (
        <li class="article rise">
          <p class="n">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</p>
          <div>
            <h2>{article.title}</h2>
            {article.text.map((paragraph) => (
              <p>{paragraph}</p>
            ))}
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell-narrow close rise">
      <p class="sign">
        If this is the sign-in you want to exist, it is being built in the open,
        one decision at a time.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/identities/">
          See how it works
          <Icon name="arrow-right" />
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={GITHUB}>
          <Icon name="github-logo" />
          Read the code
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 10vw, 7rem);
  }

  .articles {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    counter-reset: article;
  }

  .article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .n {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 2.6;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .article div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .article h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.1rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--self);
  }

  .article p:not(.n) {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .close {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  .sign {
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.6vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    .article {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
